cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Bulk2Spot, please cite it as below, together with the tools listed in docs/methods.md."
title: "Bulk2Spot: a Snakemake workflow for NanoString GeoMx DSP spatial transcriptomics"
abstract: >-
  Bulk2Spot processes GeoMx DSP RNA data from raw DCC/PKC/annotation files through
  segment and probe QC, normalization, optional RUV4 batch correction, limma-voom
  differential expression, GO/KEGG gene set enrichment, SpatialDecon cell-type
  deconvolution and GSVA signature scoring, into a self-contained HTML report.
authors:
  - family-names: "<Surname>"
    given-names: "<Name>"
# Add all contributors before publishing.
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/<OWNER>/Bulk2Spot"
keywords:
  - spatial-transcriptomics
  - geomx
  - nanostring
  - snakemake
  - differential-expression
  - deconvolution
  - bioinformatics
